---
title: Flo's Baguettes
yield: 2
image: https://spicyrranny.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/Ultimate-Guide-How-to-Make-Authentic-French-Baguettes-at-Home-1.png
time required: 13 hours
---

Mix @all-purpose flour{812%g}(about 4 cups), @salt{10%g}(about 1 heaping tsp), @active dry yeast{5%g}(about 1/2 heaping tsp), and @water{2%cups}(warm, between 100-110°F).

Cover and allow to rest for ~{12-20%hours}. Your mixture should be sticky and bubbly, and if it isn't let it rest for a bit more.

Put a #deep baking pan{} on the bottom rung of the oven filled with @water{2%cups}. 

> The goal is to cover the bottom and have enough during the baking period, but not so much that boiling it will result in spillage, so the exact amount depends on your pan.

With the water-filled baking sheet in the oven, start preheating oven to 450°F.

Generously flour your baguette pan, work surface, and your hands. 

Take about half the dough and try shaping it into a baguette shape. If it's still too sticky, massage more flour until it's no longer sticky.

Place the baguette onto the baguette pan. Repeat with remaining dough.

Score the baguettes with a sharp knife.

Once the oven is preheated, open it carefully to avoid the escaping steam. Then, place the baguette pan on the top shelf, and let it cook for ~{20-25%minutes}.

> The exact time depends on your oven, but watch for a golden crispy brown crust.